 <a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
 ## Understand the implementation
 
+Plugins register one observable readonly source per Session through trajectoryInspection. Disposing the registration restores the ordinary source. The conversation.trajectory.navigation and conversation.trajectory.toolbar slots add inspection controls without changing Chat or selecting runtime history. UiConversation.inspect assembles an independent event window through the same registered definitions.
+
+An inspection source supplies original events, optional ordered context messages, turn labels and a precise-request reader. Context records retain message role, source identity, tools, reasoning and attachments; they receive no execution time or token usage. Their display order is independent of event sequences. Real execution records retain DSH turn and step grouping. An explicit source link invokes the provider’s inspection callback. User inputs and plugin context retain their persisted source classification.
+
